==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Croco]]s spawn, delay 3.33~10 seconds<sup>100f~300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 5~10 seconds<sup>150f~300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Baa Baa]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*1 [[Le'boin]] spawns after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Pigge]]s spawn after 180 seconds<sup>5,400f</sup>, delay 20~40 seconds<sup>600f~1,200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Play this stage like you would [[Denmark (Empire of Cats)|Denmark]], but without as much time to prepare.

Start by upgrading your [[Worker Cat]]. When Croco comes near your base, spam [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Tank Cats]] and [[Axe Cat (Normal Cat)|Axe Cats]], which will also be able to kill the Baa Baas that arrive. Meanwhile, keep upgrading your Worker Cat to max level. This way your cats will slowly progress toward the enemy base, but don't let them get too close.

When Le'boin spawns, your Worker Cat should be at max level. Just try to slow down Le'boin with meatshields and Axe Cats. Thanks to all the Baa Baas, you should have a lot of money. Once Le'boin is lured close enough to your base, start spamming meatshields, Axe Cats, [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Gross Cats]], [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cats]] and [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Titan Cats]]. Use [[Bird Cat (Normal Cat)|Bird Cat]] or the [[Cat Cannon]] to clear out groups of peons.

Alternatively, you can simply rush the stage with Titan Cats, preferably at level 6 or above. Don't bother to upgrade your Worker Cat (unless your wallet's capacity isn't high enough to spawn Titan Cat).

